---
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Privacy · Diffloupe" description="Diffloupe has no trackers and is open source. Your code stays on your Mac." current="privacy">
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="prose" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="h1-doc" id="privacy-title">No trackers. Your code stays on your Mac.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Diffloupe is built to keep your work on your Mac. Here is what that means in practice.</p>
      <section class="prose-part" aria-labelledby="privacy-app">
        <span class="icon-circle"><Icon name="laptop" /></span>
        <div><h2 id="privacy-app">The app</h2><p>Diffloupe is open source, so you can read every line of what it does. It has no account and sends no usage data, and your repositories and settings stay on your Mac. It reaches a git remote only when you start a git action that needs one, such as a push.</p></div>
      </section>
      <section class="prose-part" aria-labelledby="privacy-code">
        <span class="icon-circle"><Icon name="padlock" /></span>
        <div><h2 id="privacy-code">Your code</h2><p>Your repositories, settings and history stay on your Mac. Uninstall Diffloupe… in the settings menu removes the app and everything it stored on your machine.</p></div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
